            {'after': 3, 'q': 'What did the Buddha tell Tấm to do with the fish bones after Cám killed the gudgeon?', 'options': ['Throw them into the river', 'Bury them beneath the four legs of her bed', 'Give them to the stepmother as an offering', 'Burn them at the village shrine'], 'correct': 1},
            {'after': 5, 'q': 'What form did Tấm take before living with the old tea-seller?', 'options': ['A golden oriole, a peach-wood tree, and a loom', 'A fish, a bird, and a flower', 'A shoe, a horse, and a dress', 'A well, a garden, and a lantern'], 'correct': 0},
            {'after': 6, 'q': 'How did the king recognize Tấm at the tea stall?', 'options': ['She wore her royal robes', 'He recognized the phoenix-shaped betel quid only she knew how to fold', 'A messenger told him where she was', 'She called out to him by name'], 'correct': 1},
